No problem. The context for this meeting is to allow the council members direct access to Axon's experts when it comes to the ALPR technology. Axon's approach is much different than other vendors and this is an opportunity for the council to ask whatever questions they might have, and for them to express their concerns regarding the technology and how it is managed. We are currently working on starting a trail with Axon ALPR's and we want the council to be as informed as possible. This should be framed as an executive Q&A for council. This is time sensitive so we would like to get these on the calendar for next week. I have contacted Axon and they will be confirming availability for next week by tomorrow morning. If you need more info please let me know. Thanks

Anthony

From: Martin McTaggart <mmctaggart@cityofsanmateo.org>
Sent: Wednesday, August 19, 2026 8:58 AM
To: Anthony Riccardi <ARiccardi@cityofsanmateo.org>; Ed Barberini <ebarberini@cityofsanmateo.org>; Alex Khojikian <akhojikian@cityofsanmateo.org>; Laurie Strange <strange@cityofsanmateo.org>
Subject: RE: Axon briefing for council

Good morning, Anthony,

Thank you for sending this my way; I'm happy to help facilitate Council Member participation, to help provide the Council understand the context of this, would you mind kindly sending over a blurb on the context of this presentation and what services Axon are proposing for the City?

Much appreciated,
Martin

From: Anthony Riccardi <ARiccardi@cityofsanmateo.org<mailto:ARiccardi@cityofsanmateo.org>>
Sent: Wednesday, August 19, 2026 8:38 AM
To: Ed Barberini <ebarberini@cityofsanmateo.org<mailto:ebarberini@cityofsanmateo.org>>; Alex Khojikian <akhojikian@cityofsanmateo.org<mailto:akhojikian@cityofsanmateo.org>>; Laurie Strange <strange@cityofsanmateo.org<mailto:strange@cityofsanmateo.org>>; Martin McTaggart <mmctaggart@cityofsanmateo.org<mailto:mmctaggart@cityofsanmateo.org>>
Subject: Axon briefing for council

Good morning all, Axon would like to come out to San Mateo to do an in-person executive presentation on the Axon technology and ALPR's. They are looking at some dates next week or the following week. Attached is a sample of how we can structure the day with up to two council members at a time. This would be a great opportunity for our city leaders to ask any questions they might have, and they will be hearing directly from Axon. If I could have some help with times and dates that work best with council I will work to confirm with Axon. Please let me know if you have any questions or need any further information. Thank you for your support.

Anthony



